# Project: SRE Incident Triage Agent

FastAPI backend (`backend/`) + Next.js frontend (`frontend/`).

## Backend (Python 3.12+)
- Runtime: `uv run`. Never bare `python`/`pip`/`pytest`.
- Types: annotate all public functions. Run `uv run ty check` before committing.
- Lint: `uv run ruff check`. Tests: `uv run pytest` (async, pytest-asyncio auto mode).
- Key libs: FastAPI, SQLModel/aiosqlite, Mistral SDK, Anthropic/Claude Agent SDK, structlog, stamina.

## Frontend (Next.js + TypeScript)
- Runtime: `bun`. Never bare `node`/`npm`/`npx`.
- Lint: `bunx --bun @biomejs/biome check .`. Build: `bun run build`. Tests: `bun test`.
- No `any`. Strict TypeScript only.

## Both
- TDD: write a failing test first, then implement.
- No secrets in code — use `.env` (gitignored).
- No inline comments that explain WHAT; only non-obvious WHY.
- YAGNI: build only what's asked.

## Operating the app
- `docker compose up --build` starts Phoenix (:6006), backend (:8000), frontend (:3000).
- See `skills/sre-triage/SKILL.md` for API usage: submitting incidents, checking stats, verifying integrations, debugging traces.
